sections.content:
A production deployment template uses helpers for naming, `range` for env vars, `toYaml` for passing through maps:

```yaml
# templates/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: {{ include "mychart.fullname" . }}
  labels: {{- include "mychart.labels" . | nindent 4 }}
spec:
  replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}
  selector:
    matchLabels: {{- include "mychart.selectorLabels" . | nindent 6 }}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {{- include "mychart.selectorLabels" . | nindent 8 }}
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
          image: "{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag | default .Chart.AppVersion }}"
          ports:
            - containerPort: {{ .Values.service.port }}
          env:
            {{- range $k, $v := .Values.env }}
            - name: {{ $k }}
              value: {{ $v | quote }}
            {{- end }}
          resources: {{- toYaml .Values.resources | nindent 12 }}
          livenessProbe: {{- toYaml .Values.probes.liveness | nindent 12 }}
```

And `_helpers.tpl` defines reusable templates:

```gotemplate
{{- define "mychart.fullname" -}}
{{- printf "%s-%s" .Release.Name .Chart.Name | trunc 63 | trimSuffix "-" -}}
{{- end }}

{{- define "mychart.labels" -}}
app.kubernetes.io/name: {{ .Chart.Name }}
app.kubernetes.io/instance: {{ .Release.Name }}
app.kubernetes.io/version: {{ .Chart.AppVersion | quote }}
app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: {{ .Release.Service }}
{{- end }}
```

**Rendering notes:**

- `.Values.X` comes from the merged values.
- `.Chart.X` comes from `Chart.yaml`.
- `.Release.X` is install-time: `.Release.Name`, `.Release.Namespace`, `.Release.IsUpgrade`.
- `{{- include ... }}` (with dash) trims leading whitespace; **whitespace matters** — indentation bugs are the #1 Helm template frustration.
- `required "error msg" .Values.image.repository` fails the render with a clear message if the value is missing — use it for mandatory inputs.
